specs/hal-engine-config-hooks/spec.md:16:- For a session that completes without error the hooks fire in the order `beforeSession` → `beforeUserInput` → `afterUserInput` → `beforeModelResponse` → `afterModelResponse` → `afterSession` ([validated by: fires the lifecycle hooks in documented order for a session that completes without error](../../src/config.test.ts#L132)).
specs/hal-engine-config-hooks/spec.md:24:These three properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
specs/hal-engine-config-hooks/spec.md:26:- `beforeSession` is awaited before the `try` block opens ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L91](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L91)), so a throw there escapes before the `catch`/`finally` exist and skips both `onError` and `afterSession`.
specs/hal-engine-config-hooks/spec.md:27:- The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
specs/hal-engine-config-hooks/spec.md:28:- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L148](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L148)), and is passed the `lastUsage` local — the most recent round's usage, not a sum across tool rounds, so a deployer using the hook for billing or audit under-counts every turn that ran tools.
specs/hal-engine-npm-release/tasks.md:51:- [x] T034 [P] Forward the orchestrator hooks. `src/config.ts:54` passes `maxToolRounds` and `contextConfig` to `createChatOrchestrator` and stops there, so every `OrchestratorHooks` member is unreachable through `createHalEngine` - the same one-missing-line shape as T015's `onConnect`, except the option is not declared on `HalEngineConfig` at all. Add `hooks?: OrchestratorHooks` to the `orchestrator` block, forward it, re-export the type from the package root if it is not already, and test that a hook passed through `createHalEngine` fires. Then replace § Message lifecycle hooks in `docs/getting-started.md`, which currently documents the manual-assembly workaround T019 wrote. Additive, so not a dependency of T031 - but the alternative is publishing a documented limitation with the intention of removing it immediately.
